<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Ferozepur State</h1><p class="st-meta">1763 CE – 1835 CE (approx.) · capital Ferozepur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Sikh chiefship on the Sutlej whose lapse to the British in 1835 gave them a forward base against the Sikh kingdom of Lahore.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the fall of Mughal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirhind">Sirhind</a> in 1763–64 a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> sardar took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/firozpur">Ferozepur</a>, an old town on the south bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutlej-river">Sutlej</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/firozpur">Ferozepur</a> came under British protection in 1809 as one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cis-sutlej-states">Cis-Sutlej states</a>. For much of the period it was governed by a widow of the ruling family. Little detail of its administration is recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When the line ended in 1835 the British took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/firozpur">Ferozepur</a> and turned it into a cantonment facing the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutlej-river">Sutlej</a>. It served as the main base for the Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> wars and remains a district town of Indian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="princely state, 1763 CE – 1835 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">princely state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Indian princely states</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:94.79%;width:1.43%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1763 CE – 1835 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ferozepur</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sikhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Punjabi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Firozpur</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1799&amp;focus=ferozepur-state" aria-label="Ferozepur State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6787 1321 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ferozepur State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7107 1577h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7107 1577h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day India. <a href="/atlas?year=1799&amp;focus=ferozepur-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

